            "review_text": "Getaway02653544625\n5 contributions\n0\nMust-try Central Vietnamese dishes in Cau Kieu (Phu Nhuan)\nOct 2026 • Family\nI visited Chum with my family and was quite impressed with the Central Vietnamese dishes here. My favorite dish is rice paper rolls with pork. The meat is cut into bite-sized pieces, wrapped with rice paper, rice noodles, various vegetables, and dipped in a richly flavored fermented shrimp paste sauce.\n\nWhat I like is that the side vegetables are quite diverse and you can use as much as you want. Besides the rolls, our group also tried special Chum rice rolls and some types of Hue cakes. The menu has quite a few options, so it's easier to order many dishes when going in a group or as a family.\n\nThe water is also worth trying, especially the kumquat tea and artichoke tea, the taste is quite good when eaten with rolled dishes.\n\nThe cafe space has a cozy feeling, and the staff is enthusiastic in their support. If you are looking for a rice paper roll with pork or want to try Central Vietnamese dishes in the Phu Nhuan area, Chum is a place you can check out.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten October 2, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
